xnu 0196: the CP doorbell moves to its own thread, and the ring says where a
submission stops

ring31 ends at "uc pre 71": the keepalive is healthy ("cp keepalive held up"),
there is no "uc big" line and no timeout, and the UI froze at 0 fps. The only
GPU register touched after that line is CP_RB_WPTR -- the doorbell write and the
read-back that 0188 describes as opt-in but left initialised to 1. A register
access to a stopped block never returns, and the submission runs under the user
client's lock, so the compositor waits on that lock and the whole UI stops.

The doorbell is written by a thread of its own now. If the block stops
answering, only that thread is lost, the lock is released, and the UI keeps
compositing on the CPU path (the 26 fps 0191 already gives). The ring names the
stall instead of leaving it to inference: "uc door <seq> at <dword>" before the
write, "uc door posted <seq>" after it, and a memory-only timeout that marks the
GPU stopped when neither appears. gpuasync=0 writes inline the old way.

--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_gpu.c
